# get the source code
git clone -b nov2026 git@github.com:prohaska7/tokubackup

# run with 8 parallel tests
bash test.tokubackup.bash np=8

# run tests with valgrind memcheck
bash test.tokubackup.bash runmemcheck=1

# run helgrind and drd tests
bash test.tokubackup.bash runhelgrind=1

# turn off address space randomization
setarch x86_64 -R SOME_PROGRAM

Bug #1: test6477_close_injection sometimes aborts
Bug #1: open

Bug #2:
tests with clang-18 and tsan passes
tests with clang-19 and tsan fails
tests with clang-21 and tsan fails
tests with clang-22 and tsan fails
tests with gcc-15 and tsan fails
failing tests are caused by data races protected by rwlock's.
Bug #2 resolution:
Data races appear to be false positive reports.
The TSAN option 'ignore_noninstrumented_modules=1' causes the
false positives to no longer reported.
I added some simple data races to the tokubackup tests and
shared library.  These races are reported by TSAN with the ignore
option set.
Perhaps the standard library that include rwlock's is not
instrumented by TSAN are the cause of these problems.
At least gemini thinks so.
Bug #2: closed

Bug #3: tests with tsan and gcc-14 cause FATAL unexpected memory map
the exclude_all_files tests does not compile
All tests pass when run with setarch x86_64 -R ./test
However, check_check test crashes

gcc-15 compiles with tsan and tests run
some tests fail due to bug #2.
Bug #3 closed

Bug #4:
test helgrind/open_close_6731 sometimes fails due to data race in pthread_create
running ubuntu 26.04.1 on 12 thread 8 GB memory laptop
added a helgrind suppression
Bug #4 closed
